WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.170
My phone put the message about our

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.450
match in the spam folder.

3
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.420
It said the match had moved to Saturday!

4
00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.030
Half our team turned up on Friday.

5
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.470
Today: how AI gets things

6
00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.050
wrong, and what you can do.

7
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.410
AI makes predictions, and

8
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.610
predictions can be wrong.

9
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.780
A spam filter gives every message a

10
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.460
score: how scam-like does it look?

11
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.660
Above a line, called the

12
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.540
threshold, it goes to spam.

13
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.620
There are two kinds of mistake.

14
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.340
A false alarm is when AI flags something

15
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.580
harmless, like our match message.

16
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.840
A miss is when something bad slips

17
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.300
through, like a scam in your inbox.

18
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:45.670
It’s like a referee.

19
00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.980
A strict one whistles at every touch,

20
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.820
giving fouls that weren’t fouls: false

21
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:52.340
alarms.

22
00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:56.860
A relaxed one lets real fouls go: misses.

23
00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.300
Move the line one way, and you get fewer

24
00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.920
of one mistake but more of the other.

25
00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:04.560
Quick check!

26
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.120
A fake prize message lands in your

27
00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.300
inbox, and the filter says nothing.

28
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.360
Which mistake is that?

29
00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:15.070
A miss: a real scam slipped through.

30
00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:17.730
A false alarm is the other way

31
00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.790
round: something harmless gets

32
00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.650
flagged, like my match message.

33
00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.620
So where should the line go?

34
00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.330
It depends on which mistake hurts more,

35
00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.350
and people decide that, not the computer.

36
00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.390
For school messages, hiding a real

37
00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:36.410
one, like an exam date, may be worse

38
00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:37.730
than letting a scam through.

39
00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.380
Each job may need its own line.

40
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.070
Mistakes also come from gaps in the data.

41
00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:47.350
Voice typing that learned mostly from a

42
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.970
few accents makes more mistakes with

43
00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:50.210
others.

44
00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.240
A translator that saw little of your

45
00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.140
language mixes up its words.

46
00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:57.630
That’s not your fault: the

47
00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.810
examples were missing.

48
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.620
So what can you do?

49
00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.090
Check it: look in your spam folder, or

50
00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.530
compare with a trusted source.

51
00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.830
Ask a person: a teacher, a

52
00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.050
parent, a friend.

53
00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.850
And report it: many apps have a

54
00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.150
button to say “wrong” or “not

55
00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.970
spam”, and that helps fix it.

56
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.230
In the lab, you set the threshold for a

57
00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.690
smoke alarm, which must tell real smoke

58
00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:26.350
from cooking steam, then for a spam

59
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:26.710
filter.

60
00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.690
Slide the line, and watch the counts

61
00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.950
change: caught, missed, false alarms.

62
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.940
Then find where mistakes cost least, and

63
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.060
notice it’s different for each job.

64
00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:40.820
Your turn.

65
00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:44.290
For a smoke alarm, which mistake is worse?

66
00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.280
Missing a real fire, so smoke

67
00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.020
alarms are set to go off easily.

68
00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.540
Remember: AI makes two kinds of

69
00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.260
mistake, false alarms and misses.

70
00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.990
People choose which matters more, and

71
00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:02.070
gaps in the data cause mistakes too.

72
00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.010
When AI gets it wrong: check,

73
00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.370
ask a person, report it.

74
00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:11.730
Try it yourself: this week, catch one AI

75
00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.110
mistake, like a wrong suggestion, a bad

76
00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.830
translation or a message in the wrong

77
00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:18.170
folder.

78
00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:21.150
Was it a false alarm or a miss?

79
00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.400
And what might have caused it?
